          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observation about the cups"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.408,
            0.299,
            0.765,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Probable reasons for the observation"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.393,
            0.629,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You observed that the cup under which the candle was placed, rises up (Fig. 7.3b). Why is it so? The air around the candle flame heats up. As the air in the cup warms up, it expands and occupies more space. As a result, it becomes lighter and rises up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.488,
            0.629,
            0.563
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You can experience the expansion of air on heating it by placing a partially inflated balloon in the Sun (Fig. 7.4). After the air in the balloon gets heated, it expands and the balloon becomes larger."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.634,
            0.395,
            0.903,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": [
            {
